<title>MEXICO: GCC says plans new U.S. plant.</title>
<headline>GCC says plans new U.S. plant.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican cement maker Grupo Cementos de Chihuahua (GCC) will undertake a feasibility study to decide whether to build a new plant in the U.S. state of Colorado, the company said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Building work on a new cement plant would begin in 1998 and it would have an installed capacity of one million short tons per year,&quot; a GCC statement said.</p>
<p>GCC said the plant would be built, if plans went ahead, by its U.S. subsidiary Rio Grande Portland Cement.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau +528 345 7617))</p>
